# No Retries. No Fallbacks. No Crappy Code.

Authoritative source: `plans/rules.md` §3a (Correctness — fail closed).

## Law

- **No Retries** — Do not add or retain application-level retry loops, exponential backoff, or “try again later” wrappers around failures (HTTP 5xx, timeouts, Mongo, OpenAI, GeekAPI ingest). Fail on the first failure; return the real diagnostic error; fix the root cause.
- **No Fallbacks** — Do not turn a required-operation failure into apparent success (drop fields, skip persistence, swallow exceptions, best-effort success). Intentional product processing paths are allowed only when explicit, logged, and contract-preserving — never to hide API/storage failure.
- **No Crappy Code** — Delete incorrect behavior instead of concealing it. Empty error bodies, diagnostic truncation, and silent catches are defects.

## Reject in plans and PRs

- Proposals to “retry on 502/500”, “backoff and try again”, or soft-succeed after ingest/index failure.
- Silent degradation that reports success when a required step failed.

## Prefer

- Fail closed with actionable diagnostics.
- Root-cause fixes (limits, contracts, error mapping) — never band-aid retries.
